From 281865b696e91047c30b28867397b5009c3b5aaf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roy Daniel <roydanielr@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 22:03:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] String windows: play 6 of a pedal-steel neck's 10 strings

The VG-800 host app maps a 10-string steel tuning onto a 6-string guitar by
picking a contiguous window (strings 3-8 by default). Embedded boards now
mirror that: pedal-steel tunings get a Strings chip row (1-6 | 3-8 | 4-9 |
5-10 | All 10) with a 10-dot map and the open-string voicing on every chip.

- lib/stringWindows.ts: the window table (string-number order, i0 into the
  low-first midi array) and windowedTuning() - a 6-string cut that keeps the
  parent's identity/key/copedent and recomputes the re-entrant flag per
  slice, so E9 3-8 reads low-to-high while 1-6 keeps the chromatic dip.
- App: the cut IS the baseTuning, so key, scale, chord cards, audio and the
  board all recompute for the six strings actually shown. All 10 keeps the
  full neck with the out-of-window strings drawn faded (Fretboard's new
  fadedStrings prop). Host pulls (six values) land 1:1 on the windowed
  board and map onto the window's rows in the All-10 view - they used to be
  dropped on 10-string tunings.
- embed API 1.1.0: MountOptions.stringWindows + onStringWindowChange (the
  callback is also the feature switch - without it, and in the standalone
  app, nothing changes), controller.setStringWindows({selected, disabled} |
  null) with the buffered-setter pattern the other pushes use.

Apply to guitar-fretboard-visualizer main (built bundle synced into the
VG-800 repo as fretboard/fretboard-embed.es.js).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
